<title>USA: Input/Output Q2 hurt by delayed sales.</title>
<headline>Input/Output Q2 hurt by delayed sales.</headline>
<dateline>STAFFORD, Texas 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Input/Output Inc said Thursday its second quarter results were hurt by unexpected delays in land seismic equipment sales.</p>
<p>The delayed sales are expected to close in the third quarter, the company said.</p>
<p>In the second quarter ended November 30, Input/Output earned $4.8 million or $0.11 a share on net sales of $67 million.  This compares with earnings of $14.4 million or $0.33 a share on net sales of $140 million in the second quarter last year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
